{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Revise the T10 (overlay-infra) rubric to partition routine durable-infrastructure checks away from transient de-risk experiments while retaining every existing MAJOR safety class. There is no runtime cross-criterion suppression by design, so the boundary must live in the T10 rubric text.\n\n## Work\n- Edit `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T10.md`: add this scope clause near the top: \"This overlay evaluates the DURABLE infrastructure — the IaC/config that persists. Transient, throwaway experiments used to de-risk a mechanism before committing it — their creation, isolation, and teardown — are out of scope here.\"\n- Immediately after that scope clause, add this exact co-located safety qualifier: \"This exclusion does NOT waive the four MAJOR safety classes: a transient apply that is destructive with no safeguard, grants wildcard-admin access, or commits a plaintext secret remains in scope, as does an internet- or untrusted-network-reachable transient service with unspecified human/admin authentication — flag each case.\" This preserves the current destructive-apply, wildcard-admin, plaintext-secret, and endpoint-auth protections for transient infrastructure.\n- Keep the rubric independent: T10 must not name T15 or assign scope to another overlay.\n- Add `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/plan-review-T10.eval.yaml` with ten live dataset cases. Five `pass` controls cover: a throwaway loopback probe with scoped teardown; fully specified durable infrastructure; a private-network transient probe with scoped IAM; a transient probe retrieving its secret from a secret manager; and a disposable sandbox whose teardown cannot touch shared/stateful data. Five `finding` controls cover: under-specified durable lifecycle safety; a destructive transient apply risking shared/stateful data; transient wildcard-admin access; a transient plaintext secret; and an untrusted-network transient service with unspecified human/admin authentication.\n- Add a ten-item `gold_set` with one condensed `input` plus `label` entry matching each dataset scenario: five `pass` labels and five `finding` labels, following sibling packaged plan-review specs.\n- Add offline text-contract tests in `tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py` that lock the exact scope clause, exact co-located safety qualifier, and rubric independence. Agentic finding behavior is proved separately by the live criterion eval.\n- Extend `NEW_SPECS` in `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py` with `plan-review-T10`, so the existing tests exercise strict schema validity, registered scorer discipline, dataset balance, and non-empty gold data for this spec.\n- Regenerate `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` from the registry.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The T10 rubric contains the exact durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n- [ ] The exact four-MAJOR-class safety qualifier appears immediately after the scope clause.\n- [ ] The T10 rubric does not name T15.\n- [ ] The T10 rubric does not assign scope to another overlay.\n- [ ] The packaged eval spec contains ten dataset cases split into five `pass` and five `finding` labels.\n- [ ] The packaged eval spec contains ten matching `gold_set` entries split into five `pass` and five `finding` labels.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py` registers `plan-review-T10` in `NEW_SPECS`.\n- [ ] The strict packaged-spec tests pass for `plan-review-T10`.\n- [ ] The offline T10 text-contract tests pass and assert the exact scope clause.\n- [ ] The offline T10 text-contract tests pass and assert the exact safety qualifier.\n- [ ] The offline T10 text-contract tests pass and assert the absence of any T15 reference.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports pass for the scoped throwaway loopback-probe case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports pass for the fully specified durable-infrastructure case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports pass for the private-network scoped-IAM transient case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports pass for the secret-manager transient case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports pass for the sandboxed-teardown transient case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports finding for the under-specified durable-lifecycle case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports finding for the destructive transient-apply case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports finding for the transient wildcard-admin case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports finding for the transient plaintext-secret case.\n- [ ] `rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3` reports finding for the untrusted-network transient-service case.\n- [ ] `rebar explain T10` renders the durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n- [ ] `rebar explain T10` renders the four-MAJOR-class safety qualifier.\n- [ ] The regenerated T10 guide section renders the durable-infrastructure scope clause.\n- [ ] The regenerated T10 guide section renders the four-MAJOR-class safety qualifier.\n\n## Testing\n- Run `.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/plan_review/test_criteria_blocking.py tests/unit/test_new_eval_specs.py -q`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/rebar criteria eval T10 --runs 3`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry regenerate-criteria-guide`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/python -m rebar.llm.plan_review.registry validate-routing`.\n- Run `.venv/bin/rebar explain T10` and verify the rendered clause and qualifier."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786552983542300001,"uuid":"80d87961-caec-460b-be42-3159eb79567c"}